  "interpretation": "<table style=\"width: 77.1484%;\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"width: 45.539%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>IgE Level (kU/L)</strong></span></th>\n<th style=\"width: 54.368%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Interpretation</strong></span></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 45.539%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">&lt; 0.35</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 54.368%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Negative</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 45.539%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">0.35 &ndash; 0.70</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 54.368%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Borderline</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 45.539%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">0.71 &ndash; 3.50</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 54.368%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Low-level sensitization</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 45.539%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">3.51 &ndash; 17.50</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 54.368%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Moderate sensitization</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 45.539%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">17.51 &ndash; 50.00</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 54.368%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">High-level sensitization</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 45.539%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">&gt; 50.00</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 54.368%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Very high sensitization</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3 data-start=\"2058\" data-end=\"2074\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong data-start=\"2062\" data-end=\"2074\">Remarks:</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start=\"2076\" data-end=\"2467\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"2076\" data-end=\"2185\">\n<p data-start=\"2078\" data-end=\"2185\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">A positive result indicates <strong data-start=\"2106\" data-end=\"2142\">sensitization to gluten proteins</strong> but <strong data-start=\"2147\" data-end=\"2182\">does not confirm celiac disease</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"2186\" data-end=\"2334\">\n<p data-start=\"2188\" data-end=\"2334\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">This test should be interpreted in conjunction with clinical findings and other tests (e.g., <strong data-start=\"2281\" data-end=\"2293\">Anti-tTG</strong>, <strong data-start=\"2295\" data-end=\"2320\">Endomysial antibodies</strong>, <strong data-start=\"2322\" data-end=\"2332\">Biopsy</strong>).</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\" data-start=\"2335\" data-end=\"2467\">\n<p data-start=\"2337\" data-end=\"2467\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">For suspected <strong data-start=\"2351\" data-end=\"2369\">celiac disease</strong>, consider <strong data-start=\"2380\" data-end=\"2396\">Anti-tTG IgA</strong>, <strong data-start=\"2398\" data-end=\"2434\">Deamidated Gliadin Peptide (DGP)</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"2440\" data-end=\"2459\">total serum IgA</strong> levels.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
